  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197510",
      "title": "Managing Colors Globally",
      "lectureOrder": 63,
      "videoOrder": 60,
      "sourceHash": "d28d077973f69d171129e9ba61b5a402c310efaaedd4fdd02f94b0c3ed86bf0f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.02,
          "end": 3.38,
          "en": "Now in the previous lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.38,
          "end": 5.22,
          "en": "we added this title component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.22,
          "end": 6.82,
          "en": "And by doing so we made sure that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.82,
          "end": 9.31,
          "en": "we had this reusable title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.31,
          "end": 11.68,
          "en": "But speaking of reusability",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.68,
          "end": 15.65,
          "en": "and repeating certain things and settings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.65,
          "end": 17.81,
          "en": "you might have noticed that these colors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.81,
          "end": 21.69,
          "en": "which I'm using are used in different places of the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.69,
          "end": 24.1,
          "en": "I'm using colors in the Start GameScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.1,
          "end": 26.52,
          "en": "in the primary button component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.52,
          "end": 28.72,
          "en": "in the title component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.72,
          "end": 32.26,
          "en": "And having all these colors in all these places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.26,
          "end": 33.52,
          "en": "is not ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.52,
          "end": 36.92,
          "en": "It's just as in web development with CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.92,
          "end": 39.51,
          "en": "If you're using the same colors in different places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 42.79,
          "en": "which you typically are, repeating them manually is annoying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.79,
          "end": 46.26,
          "en": "because you always have to copy the exact same hex codes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.26,
          "end": 48.79,
          "en": "and if you would change to color at some point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.79,
          "end": 51.83,
          "en": "and even if it's just a slight change, a small change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.83,
          "end": 54.58,
          "en": "you would have to apply that in different files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.58,
          "end": 57.153,
          "en": "of your project, which of course is not great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.18,
          "end": 61.45,
          "en": "Now in CSS, you could solve this problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.45,
          "end": 65.64,
          "en": "by using CSS variables, CSS custom properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.64,
          "end": 68.4,
          "en": "But this feature doesn't exist with React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.4,
          "end": 71.03999999999999,
          "en": "because we're not using CSS here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.03999999999999,
          "end": 74.05,
          "en": "Therefore what is commonly done in React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.05,
          "end": 76.48,
          "en": "is that you create a helper file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.48,
          "end": 79.74,
          "en": "that exposes certain constant values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.74,
          "end": 81.453,
          "en": "like the colors you're using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.34,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "And for this I'll add a new folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 88.02,
          "en": "which you could name Util for utility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.02,
          "end": 91.1,
          "en": "or constants or whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.1,
          "end": 92.75999999999999,
          "en": "And I'll go for constants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.75999999999999,
          "end": 96.453,
          "en": "because I'll manage some constant reused values in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.53999999999999,
          "end": 101.313,
          "en": "and then I'll add a colors JS file in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 106.19,
          "en": "And in this file, I'll create a colors constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.19,
          "end": 109.13300000000001,
          "en": "which is just a regular Javascript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.02000000000001,
          "end": 112.00999999999999,
          "en": "But in this object, I'm now going to set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.00999999999999,
          "end": 115.53,
          "en": "various properties which I'll reuse over and over again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.53,
          "end": 117.14,
          "en": "throughout this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.14,
          "end": 119.27000000000001,
          "en": "For example, a primary color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.27000000000001,
          "end": 121.7,
          "en": "And since I plan on managing multiple shades",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.7,
          "end": 125.84,
          "en": "of the primary color, I'll name this primary500.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.84,
          "end": 127.38,
          "en": "It doesn't have to be 500,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.38,
          "end": 129.95,
          "en": "it could be primary 1 and 2 and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.95,
          "end": 134.45,
          "en": "but I will indicate how saturated or dark a shade is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.45,
          "end": 139.253,
          "en": "by higher or lower numbers after the main property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.11,
          "end": 145.11,
          "en": "Now my primary500 number could be this primary plum color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.91,
          "end": 151.07999999999998,
          "en": "which I have here in my by button for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 155.69299999999998,
          "en": "So in colors, I'll set this here as my primary500 color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.3,
          "end": 162.3,
          "en": "Now we can export this colors constant here as a default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.21,
          "end": 166.38,
          "en": "and import it in all the places where this color is needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.38,
          "end": 168.39,
          "en": "like in the primary button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.11599999999999,
          "end": 171.89,
          "en": "There, we also have a different shade by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.89,
          "end": 173.49,
          "en": "because of the ripple effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.49,
          "end": 175.43,
          "en": "It's a slightly darker shade,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.43,
          "end": 180.43,
          "en": "so I'll go to my colors constant and also add primary600",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.82,
          "end": 183.823,
          "en": "to store this shade here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.17,
          "end": 187.03,
          "en": "And then in primary button as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.03,
          "end": 191.8,
          "en": "we can import colors from going up one level,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.8,
          "end": 194.5,
          "en": "diving into the constant folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.5,
          "end": 196.74,
          "en": "and then into the colors file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.74,
          "end": 199.06,
          "en": "and now here we wanna use the darker shade,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.06,
          "end": 203.863,
          "en": "so I access colors.primary600 to use that constant value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.18,
          "end": 206.53,
          "en": "And down here in the style sheet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.53,
          "end": 208.7,
          "en": "we can use this constant array as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.7,
          "end": 211.503,
          "en": "and I can access colors primary500.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.43,
          "end": 215.99,
          "en": "And if we would change the colors here in this colors file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.99,
          "end": 219.09,
          "en": "those changes would be applied to all the components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.09,
          "end": 221.92000000000002,
          "en": "where we import this constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.92000000000002,
          "end": 224.81,
          "en": "That's the advantage of using this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.81,
          "end": 228.31,
          "en": "Because now we can manage the colors in one global place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 228.31,
          "end": 231.14,
          "en": "and then use these colors in multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.14,
          "end": 234.43,
          "en": "and changes therefore only have to be made in one place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 234.43,
          "end": 235.69299999999998,
          "en": "instead of many places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
